Task 2: Enable Retries for Transient Failures
Subtask 2.1: Create a Failure Simulator Service
Create a service that randomly fails to simulate transient errors:
cat << 'EOF' > failure-simulator.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: failure-simulator
  namespace: resilient-services
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: failure-simulator
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: failure-simulator
        version: v1
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: failure-sim
        image: python:3.9-slim
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
        command: ["python", "-c"]
        args:
        - |
          import http.server
          import socketserver
          import random
          import time
          from urllib.parse import urlparse, parse_qs
          
          class FailureHandler(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):
              def do_GET(self):
                  parsed_url = urlparse(self.path)
                  query_params = parse_qs(parsed_url.query)
                  failure_rate = float(query_params.get('failure_rate', [0.3])[0])
                  
                  if random.random() < failure_rate:
                      self.send_response(503)
                      self.send_header('Content-type', 'application/json')
                      self.end_headers()
                      response = '{"error": "Service temporarily unavailable"}'
                      self.wfile.write(response.encode())
                  else:
                      self.send_response(200)
                      self.send_header('Content-type', 'application/json')
                      self.end_headers()
                      response = f'{{"message": "Success", "timestamp": "{time.time()}"}}'
                      self.wfile.write(response.encode())
          
          PORT = 8080
          with socketserver.TCPServer(("", PORT), FailureHandler) as httpd:
              print(f"Failure simulator running on port {PORT}")
              httpd.serve_forever()
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: failure-simulator
  namespace: resilient-services
spec:
  selector:
    app: failure-simulator
  ports:
  - port: 8080
    targetPort: 8080
  type: ClusterIP
EOF
Deploy the failure simulator:
kubectl apply -f failure-simulator.yaml
Subtask 2.2: Configure Retry Policies
Create a VirtualService with retry configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > retry-virtualservice.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: VirtualService
metadata:
  name: failure-simulator-retry
  namespace: resilient-services
spec:
  hosts:
  - failure-simulator
  http:
  - timeout: 10s
    retries:
      attempts: 3
      perTryTimeout: 2s
      retryOn: 5xx,reset,connect-failure,refused-stream
      retryRemoteLocalities: true
    route:
    - destination:
        host: failure-simulator
        port:
          number: 8080
EOF
Apply the retry configuration:
kubectl apply -f retry-virtualservice.yaml
Subtask 2.3: Configure Circuit Breaker Pattern
Create a DestinationRule with circuit breaker settings:
cat << 'EOF' > circuit-breaker-destinationrule.yaml
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: DestinationRule
metadata:
  name: failure-simulator-circuit-breaker
  namespace: resilient-services
spec:
  host: failure-simulator
  trafficPolicy:
    outlierDetection:
      consecutiveGatewayErrors: 3
      consecutive5xxErrors: 3
      interval: 30s
      baseEjectionTime: 30s
      maxEjectionPercent: 50
      minHealthPercent: 30
    connectionPool:
      tcp:
        maxConnections: 10
      http:
        http1MaxPendingRequests: 10
        maxRequestsPerConnection: 2
        maxRetries: 3
        connectTimeout: 30s
        h2UpgradePolicy: UPGRADE
EOF
Apply the circuit breaker configuration:
kubectl apply -f circuit-breaker-destinationrule.yaml
